\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\kerning2\i\f0\fs22 Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced a College Application class on July 15\kerning0 , 2026,\kerning2  at 5:30 \kerning0 PM\kerning2  and reported that the Summer Discovery Program continues for another month, with prizes available after completing six books or activities and entry into countywide weekly drawings.\kerning0\line\line\kerning2 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell invited the community to attend the Composting Class at the Manhattan Beach Botanical Garden in Polliwog Park on Saturday, July 11, 2026, at 10:00 \kerning0 AM.\line\line\kerning2 Downtown Manhattan Beach Business & Professional Association Executive Director Kelly Stroman announced the upcoming 20th anniversary celebration of the Manhattan Beach Farmers Market on July 21\kerning0 , 2026,\kerning2  from 11\kerning0 :00 AM\kerning2  to 3\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2 , noting special activities and longtime vendors participating. She encouraged the community and City representatives to attend.\kerning0\line\line\kerning2 Planning Manager Adam Finestone announced the final community open house to preview conceptual designs for the Project Pulse effort,\kerning0  \kerning2 at the Joslyn\kerning0  Community\kerning2  Center scheduled for Wednesday, July 15\kerning0 , 2026,\kerning2  from 6\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2  to 8\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2 , and encouraged community participation.\kerning0\line\line\kerning2 Mayor Franklin invited the community to attend Coffee with the Mayor at Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf on Thursday, July 9, 2026, at 9:00 \kerning0 AM\kerning2 , and at Verve Coffee on Thursday, July 16, 2026, at 9:00 \kerning0 AM.\line\line\kerning2 Councilmember Howorth recognized City staff, first responders, and the communications team for their extensive work supporting \kerning0 FIFA \kerning2 World Cup\kerning0  \kerning2 related activities, noting successful public safety efforts and strong community engagement throughout the event.\kerning0\line\line\kerning2 Mayor Franklin added that visiting guests expressed high praise for the City\rquote s beauty and cleanliness, noting how much they enjoyed their experience, and thanked staff for their efforts.\kerning0\line\line\kerning2 Councilmember Charelian thanked Public Safety staff for their work during recent major events, including the \kerning0 Nation\rquote s\kerning2  250th anniversary, Fourth of July, and the nearby Hermosa Beach Ironman, noting their ongoing efforts to keep the community safe.\kerning0\line\line\pard\kerning2 Mayor Pro Tem Tarnay noted that copies of the U\kerning0 nited States\kerning2  Constitution are available in the lobby\kerning0  in front of City Council Chambers\kerning2  for residents and thanked staff for their work on the commemorative materials and activities celebrating the nation\rquote s 250th anniversary.\cf1\kerning0\i0\f1\fs24\par
